# Linda Design System — Component Rules

## 1. Slot pattern is the primary composition model

Every Linda composable must expose its variable regions as `@Composable` slots, never as raw data or strings. Data params are only acceptable for primitive values that drive internal behaviour (e.g. `expanded: Boolean`, `enabled: Boolean`, `onClick`).

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — string locks the label to plain text
fun LindaFoo(label: String)

// ✅ GOOD — slot lets the caller use any composable
fun LindaFoo(label: @Composable (() -> Unit)? = null)
```

### Scope interfaces for multi-slot DSLs

When a composable accepts repeated child elements (chips, segments, items), expose them through a `@Composable` function inside a scope interface — not through a `List<T>`.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD
fun <T> LindaFoo(items: List<T>, itemLabel: (T) -> String)

// ✅ GOOD
interface LindaFooScope {
    @Composable
    fun LindaFooItem(selected: Boolean, onClick: () -> Unit, content: @Composable () -> Unit)
}

@Composable
fun LindaFoo(content: @Composable LindaFooScope.() -> Unit)
```

The composable creates a private `LindaFooScopeImpl` internally and invokes the lambda with it as receiver. Callers never see the impl class.

### Required composable slots

Every Linda component must declare these slots when the concept applies:

| Slot | Type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `label` | `@Composable (() -> Unit)?` | Floating or section label |
| `helper` | `@Composable (() -> Unit)?` | Helper / error text below the component |
| `placeholder` | `@Composable (() -> Unit)?` | Empty-state hint inside a field |
| `content` | `@Composable (() -> Unit)?` | Primary selected-value display |
| `leadingContent` | `@Composable (() -> Unit)?` | Leading icon or decoration |

---

## 2. All visual values must come from Linda tokens

Never use raw literals for colors, dimensions, typography, or borders inside a Linda composable. Always read from `LindaTheme.*`.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD
Text(text = label, color = Color(0xFFB0B0B0), fontSize = 14.sp)
Box(modifier = Modifier.padding(8.dp).clip(RoundedCornerShape(12.dp)))

// ✅ GOOD
Text(text = label, color = LindaTheme.colors.textMuted,
     style = LindaTheme.typography.labelSmall)
Box(modifier = Modifier
    .padding(LindaTheme.spacing.md)
    .clip(LindaTheme.borders.radiusMd))
```

### Token namespaces

| Namespace | Examples |
|---|---|
| `LindaTheme.colors.*` | `textPrimary`, `textMuted`, `accentLime`, `accentGold`, `surfaceGlass`, `borderGlass`, `glowLime`, `statusError` |
| `LindaTheme.spacing.*` | `xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl` |
| `LindaTheme.typography.*` | `displaySmall`, `bodyMedium`, `bodySmall`, `labelSmall`, `labelLarge` |
| `LindaTheme.borders.*` | `radiusMd`, `radiusFull` |

---

## 3. Size presets follow the factory companion pattern

Size configuration classes use `private constructor` + `@Composable` companion factory functions. Factories must read dimensions from `LindaTheme.spacing.*` — never from raw `Dp` literals.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — raw literals inside factory
class LindaFooSize private constructor(internal val paddingV: Dp, internal val paddingH: Dp) {
    companion object {
        fun small()  = LindaFooSize(8.dp,  12.dp)   // ← raw Dp, violates rule #2
        fun medium() = LindaFooSize(12.dp, 16.dp)
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD — factories are @Composable so they can read LindaTheme tokens
class LindaFooSize private constructor(internal val paddingV: Dp, internal val paddingH: Dp) {
    companion object {
        @Composable
        fun small()  = LindaFooSize(paddingV = LindaTheme.spacing.xs, paddingH = LindaTheme.spacing.sm)
        @Composable
        fun medium() = LindaFooSize(paddingV = LindaTheme.spacing.sm, paddingH = LindaTheme.spacing.md)
        @Composable
        fun large()  = LindaFooSize(paddingV = LindaTheme.spacing.md, paddingH = LindaTheme.spacing.lg)
    }
}
```

---

## 4. Enabled / disabled state is always a param, never inferred

```kotlin
// ✅ Always declare separate enabled flags when two actions exist independently
fun LindaStepper(
    incrementEnabled: Boolean = true,
    decrementEnabled: Boolean = true,
)
```

---

## 5. Accessibility

Every interactive Linda composable must include an `accessibilityValue: String = ""` param that is wired to `semantics { contentDescription = accessibilityValue }` on the relevant node.
